{{also|مشک|م س ك}}
==Arabic==

===Etymology 1===
From the root {{ar-root|م|س|ك}}.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I|a|u,i}}

# to [[grab]], [[grasp]], [[clutch]], [[clasp]], [[seize]], [[take hold]]
# to [[hold]]
# to [[stick]], [[cling]], [[adhere]], [[hang on]]
<!-- Evidently only in particular expressions
# to [[keep]] ''(the books, accounts, etc.)''
# to [[take]] ''(charge, control, etc.)''
-->

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I|a|u,i|passive=y|vn=مَسْك}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II}}

# to have someone [[seize]] or [[hold]] something

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|مَسْك|m}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|مَسَكَ|form=I}}
# [[seizure]], [[grip]], [[hold]]
# [[keeping]] ''(bookkeeping, etc.)''

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|مَسْك}}

====Adjective====
{{ar-adj|مُسُك|f=مُسُكَة|pl=مُسَكَة}}

# [[grasping]], [[greedy]], [[avaricious]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-adj|مُسُك|pl=مُسَكَة}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*mašk-}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|مَسْك|m|pl=مُسُوك}}

# recently [[cut]] [[hide]] of a [[newborn|new-born]] [[goat]], [[scalp]] of a [[neonate]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|مَسْك|pl=مُسُوك}}

=====Alternative forms=====
* {{alter|ar|مَسْكَة}}

===Etymology 3===
From {{bor|ar|pal||tr=mwšk'|ts=mušk|t=musk}} ({{cog|fa|مشک|tr=mošk|t=musk}}), from {{der|ar|sa|मुष्क|t=testicle, scrotum}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|مِسْك|m|g2=f}}

# [[musk]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|82|25-26|passage=يُسۡقَوۡنَ مِن رَّحِيقࣲ مَّخۡتُومٍ &#1757; خِتَـٰمُهُۥ '''مِسۡكࣱۚ'''{{...}}|subst=يُسۡقَوۡنَ مِن رَّحِيقࣲ مَّخۡتُومٍ/يُسْقَوْنَ مِنْ رَحِيقٍ مَخْتُومٍ,خِتَـٰمُهُۥ '''مِسۡكࣱۚ'''/خِتَامُهُو '''مِسْكٌ'''}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|مِسْك}}

